{title: O Worship the King}
{artist: Robert Grant (1779-1838)}
{key: G}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
O [G]worship the [Em]King all [C]glorious a[G]bove,
O [G]gratefully [Em]sing His [A]power and His [D]love;
Our [G]Shield and De[Em]fender, the [C]Ancient of [G]Days,
Pa[C]vilioned in [G]splendor, and [D]girded with [G]praise.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 2}
O [G]tell of His [Em]might, O [C]sing of His [G]grace,
Whose [G]robe is the [Em]light, whose [A]canopy [D]space;
His [G]chariots of [Em]wrath the deep [C]thunderclouds [G]form,
And [C]dark is His [G]path on the [D]wings of the [G]storm.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 3}
Thy [G]bountiful [Em]care what [C]tongue can re[G]cite?
It [G]breathes in the [Em]air, it [A]shines in the [D]light;
It [G]streams from the [Em]hills, it de[C]scends to the [G]plain,
And [C]sweetly dis[G]tills in the [D]dew and the [G]rain.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 4}
Frail [G]children of [Em]dust, and [C]feeble as [G]frail,
In [G]Thee do we [Em]trust, nor [A]find Thee to [D]fail;
Thy [G]mercies how [Em]tender, how [C]firm to the [G]end,
Our [C]Maker, De[G]fender, Re[D]deemer, and [G]Friend.
{eov}
